**Ghana Smart Service Operations Optimizer**

Data Dictionary — Dataset Package

*DCIT 204/308 Joint DSA Semester Project · Team SEG26-41 SYNERGY · Local context: University of Ghana, Legon campus service hub*

# 1. Overview

This dataset seeds the six-table SQLite database (schema.sql) for the Ghana Smart Service Operations Optimizer. It models a campus service-dispatch platform for the University of Ghana, Legon: hostels, academic buildings, admin offices, security posts and other campus locations connected by roads/paths, with service requests (IT support, security, facility repair, medical, etc.) that need to be prioritised and assigned to resources (vans, riders, crews, ambulance).

# 2. Record counts vs brief minimums

| **Entity** | **Minimum required** | **Records provided** | **Status** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Locations | 50 | 53 | Met |
| Roads / edges | 100 | 137 | Met |
| Service requests | 300 | 320 | Met |
| Resources | 30 | 32 | Met |
| Algorithm runs | 30 | 50 | Met |

## 3.1 locations  (53 records)

Every node in the campus service network (hostels, academic buildings, admin offices, security posts, retail points, sports facilities, shuttle stops, health facilities).

| **Field** | **Type / constraint** | **Description** | **Example** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| location_id | TEXT (PK) | Unique location code, format L### (e.g. L001). | - |
| name | TEXT | Real / realistic local name of the place on campus. | Commonwealth Hall |
| area | TEXT | Campus sub-area / zone. | Legon, Haatso |
| location_type | TEXT (enum) | One of: Hostel, Academic, Library, Health, Admin, Security, Retail, Sports, Shuttle. | Hostel |
| x_coord | REAL | Latitude (or local grid X). | 5.6531 |
| y_coord | REAL | Longitude (or local grid Y). | 0.1857 |

## 3.2 roads  (137 records)

Weighted edges connecting locations - the graph that BFS/DFS/Dijkstra/Prim/Kruskal run over. Modelled as directed rows but the application layer treats the network as traversable both ways.

| **Field** | **Type / constraint** | **Description** | **Example** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| road_id | TEXT (PK) | Unique road/edge code, format R### (e.g. R001). | - |
| from_location_id | TEXT (FK -> locations) | Origin node of the edge. | L001 |
| to_location_id | TEXT (FK -> locations) | Destination node of the edge. | L049 |
| distance_km | REAL, > 0 | Physical distance between the two locations. | 0.10 |
| travel_time_min | INTEGER, > 0 | Estimated travel time on foot/vehicle. | 1 |
| condition_weight | REAL, >= 0.5 | Multiplier reflecting road condition; ~1.0 = good, higher = worse (traffic, potholes, construction). | 1.09 |

## 3.3 service_requests  (320 records)

Jobs to be queued, prioritised, searched and sorted by the dispatch engine - the main workload for the priority queue, hash table index, and scheduling algorithms.

| **Field** | **Type / constraint** | **Description** | **Example** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| request_id | TEXT (PK) | Unique request code, format Q### (e.g. Q001). | - |
| source_location_id | TEXT (FK -> locations) | Where the request originates. | L017 |
| destination_location_id | TEXT (FK -> locations) | Where the resource must go / deliver to. | L016 |
| category | TEXT | Service category. | Security, IT Support, Facility Repair, Electrical, Plumbing, Medical, Maintenance, Cleaning, Document, Lab Equipment, Shuttle Request, Waste Pickup |
| urgency | INTEGER, 1-5 | Priority level used by the priority queue / heap (5 = most urgent). | 2 |
| time_submitted | TEXT (ISO 8601) | Timestamp the request was logged. | 2026-07-05T16:54 |
| deadline | TEXT (ISO 8601) | Timestamp by which the request must be resolved (always after time_submitted). | 2026-07-05T22:54 |
| status | TEXT (enum) | One of: NEW, IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETED, CANCELLED. | COMPLETED |

## 3.4 resources  (32 records)

Vans, riders, crews and other assets that can be assigned to a service request.

| **Field** | **Type / constraint** | **Description** | **Example** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| resource_id | TEXT (PK) | Unique resource code (e.g. R001, V001, A003). | - |
| resource_type | TEXT | What kind of resource. | IT Support Rider, Electrician Team, Ambulance, Plumbing Team, Facilities Van, Security Patrol Vehicle, Shuttle Bus, Cleaning Crew, Maintenance Van, Courier Rider |
| home_location_id | TEXT (FK -> locations) | Base/depot location for this resource. | L009 |
| capacity | INTEGER, > 0 | How many requests/passengers it can serve at once. | 1 |
| availability_status | TEXT (enum) | One of: AVAILABLE, BUSY, MAINTENANCE. | AVAILABLE |

## 3.5 algorithm_runs  (50 records)

Empirical timing/memory measurements produced by Module M10 (the efficiency lab) - search, sort, hash table, heap and graph experiments across increasing input sizes.

| **Field** | **Type / constraint** | **Description** | **Example** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| run_id | TEXT (PK) | Unique run code, format RUN### (e.g. RUN001). | - |
| algorithm_name | TEXT | Which algorithm/structure was measured. | LinearSearch, BinarySearch, SelectionSort, MergeSort, QuickSort, HashTable, Dijkstra, etc. |
| input_size | INTEGER, > 0 | Number of records/keys used for this run. | 1000 |
| time_ns | INTEGER, >= 0 | Measured runtime in nanoseconds (average of 3 runs). | 43965 |
| memory_kb | INTEGER, >= 0 | Measured memory footprint in kilobytes. | 118 |
| date_run | TEXT (date) | Date the experiment was run. | 2026-07-15 |

## 3.6 audit_events  (0 records)

Stack-based undo log / system event trail (backed by the custom MyStack structure). Populated at runtime by the application, not seeded from CSV - kept empty in the seed data on purpose.

| **Field** | **Type / constraint** | **Description** | **Example** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| event_id | INTEGER (PK, autoincrement) | Auto-generated event number. | - |
| event_type | TEXT | e.g. ASSIGN, UNDO_ASSIGN, STATUS_CHANGE, DELETE. | ASSIGN |
| entity_type | TEXT | Which table the event refers to. | service_requests |
| entity_id | TEXT | ID of the affected row. | Q001 |
| details / event_time | TEXT | Free-text details plus an ISO timestamp defaulted by SQLite. | (auto) |

# 4. Referential integrity

roads.from_location_id / to_location_id, service_requests.source_location_id / destination_location_id, and resources.home_location_id all reference locations.location_id. Foreign keys are enforced by SQLite (PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON) and independently checked by the CSV loader before insertion — see Module M2 (CsvLoader.java / ValidationReport.java) for validation evidence.

